d.3. Key Takeaways & Lessons Learned

1. What did the successful case do right 
   Nestlé carefully planned each stage, engaged employees early, conducted extensive testing, and worked closely with the vendor to ensure the system met business needs.  

2. What went wrong in the failed case  
   Target Canada rushed the implementation, failed to conduct proper testing, encountered data migration issues, and underestimated the complexity of integrating SAP with its supply chain, leading to severe disruptions.  
3. How can future implementations avoid similar failures 
   Future enterprise system implementations should prioritize thorough planning, realistic timelines, extensive testing, proper data migration, employee training, and strong vendor support. 

e. Insights & Recommendations
e.1. Best Practices for Successful Enterprise System Implementation  
For a successful enterprise system rollout, organizations should develop a clear implementation plan, involve employees early, and ensure the system is well-suited to their needs. Conducting thorough testing, providing comprehensive training, and managing data migration effectively are crucial steps. Additionally, securing ongoing vendor support and monitoring system performance post-launch can help maintain smooth operations.  
e.2. Strategies to Avoid Failure
To prevent failure, companies should set achievable timelines, avoid rushing the implementation, and allocate sufficient time for testing and training. Engaging key employees during development ensures the system aligns with business needs. Proper data validation and rigorous testing before deployment help avoid critical errors. Furthermore, companies should establish strong vendor partnerships for ongoing support.  
e.3. Future Research Opportunities
Future studies can explore ways to enhance enterprise system selection and implementation strategies, analyze emerging technologies that simplify integration, and investigate best practices for data migration. Research can also focus on measuring the long-term impact of ERP systems on business performance and identifying cost-effective solutions for small and medium-sized enterprises. Additionally, industry-specific ERP adoption challenges can be examined to develop tailored implementation approaches.
